SCOPE OF THE ABOVE

The MIT licence above covers only what the 1.6 port added, which is the whole
of the C# in Source/ as it now stands:

  - the one thing 1.6 broke: FloatMenuOptionProvider_TakeSkateboard, replacing
    a Harmony patch on FloatMenuMakerMap.ChoicesAtFor, a method 1.6 deleted
  - the four fixes to defects that predate 1.6: the doubled PatchAll, the
    terrain list that existed in three copies of which one had fallen behind,
    the Shredder trait left on a pawn who leaves the map, and the removal of a
    caravan patch that never ran and leaked a Thing reference per arrival
  - the rewriting around them: one renderer postfix instead of two, the terrain
    list resolved to TerrainDef once at load instead of a string array rebuilt
    and searched on every tick of every pawn, and a publicised field instead of
    a Traverse lookup per pawn per frame
  - the English keyed strings and the French translation
  - the packaging and the documentation

IT DOES NOT COVER THE ORIGINAL MOD. The folding skateboard, the Shredder trait,
the recipe, the research and skill gates, the movement bonus, the contents of
the list of surfaces you can ride on, the draw offsets, and the four textures
are SilkCircuit's work, reused here:

  https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3414678101

SilkCircuit never declared a licence for them, so none is granted here and none
can be. They are redistributed under the usual practice for abandoned mods -
explicit credit, a link to the original, and removal on request.
About/Preview.png is theirs as it stands, and the four textures are theirs byte
for byte; only their file names changed.

If SilkCircuit asks for this to be taken down, it comes down. Immediately, and
without discussion.

ATTRIBUTION.md records what was taken and what was changed.
